Thai script support: UI font and video-export registry

Nothing in the project's font stack covers Thai. Inter, loaded in app/layout.tsx
for the UI chrome, ships latin, latin-ext, greek, cyrillic and vietnamese — the
comment above that import records the same problem being fixed for Cyrillic and
Vietnamese once already. Thai therefore fell through to whatever font the host
OS supplies, which differs per machine and mixes typefaces mid-sentence against
the Latin around it.

The export path is worse than inconsistent: it is broken. Video export bundles
its own fonts, and the two registries between them cover CJK (noto-cjk) and
cyrillic + arabic (noto-script-fonts). Thai is in neither, so Thai narration
renders as tofu in an exported MP4 rather than merely in a different typeface.

Both are addressed the way the project already does it:

- app/layout.tsx imports the 400 and 700 weights of @fontsource/noto-sans-thai.
  These are the per-subset files carrying `unicode-range`, matching Inter's own
  loading, so the browser fetches the Thai face only when Thai glyphs appear and
  falls through per glyph in mixed Thai/Latin runs. Measured on a running dev
  server: two of the six declared faces load (400 and 700 Thai), the latin and
  latin-ext siblings are never fetched, and `document.fonts.check(..., 'ก')`
  answers true while the same check for 'A' answers false.
- app/globals.css adds 'Noto Sans Thai' to --font-sans after Inter.
- The video-export script gains a thai face descriptor and 'thai' joins the
  script list in the three places that enumerate it.

Not in this patch, on purpose:

- pnpm-lock.yaml. Adding one package churned 2,934 lines of it, and a lockfile
  hunk conflicts on every upstream dependency change. Run `pnpm install` after
  applying instead.
- lib/video-export/emit-hyperframes/noto-script-font-assets.ts and
  public/vendor/video-export/fonts/noto-sans-thai-thai-400-normal.woff2, which
  `pnpm run gen:video-export-noto-script-fonts` produces.

Apply, then: pnpm install && pnpm run gen:video-export-noto-script-fonts

